WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.542 --> 00:00:15.723
Mandy looked in awe at the men.

2
00:00:17.103 --> 00:00:20.825
They were two of the most famous figures in American history.

3
00:00:22.106 --> 00:00:26.208
John Adams would become the second president of the United States.

4
00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:32.462
And Paul Revere would make a famous midnight ride from Boston to Lexington.

5
00:00:33.723 --> 00:00:38.705
He'd ride to warn of the first British attack in the American Revolution.

6
00:00:38.725 --> 00:00:44.147
"I am told you have a message for me," said John Adams to Vinnie.

7
00:00:45.727 --> 00:00:48.929
Vinnie trembled nervously as he gave him the paper.

8
00:00:50.349 --> 00:00:53.771
Both men read the note and spoke in low voices.

9
00:00:53.791 --> 00:00:56.512
"Thank you for delivering this.

10
00:00:56.916 --> 00:01:00.217
John Hancock needs our help," said Paul Revere.

11
00:01:00.237 --> 00:01:02.198
"Can I help?"

12
00:01:02.698 --> 00:01:03.298
asked Vinnie.

13
00:01:04.678 --> 00:01:06.579
Adams patted Vinnie on the shoulder.

14
00:01:06.599 --> 00:01:10.260
"You are very brave," he said.

15
00:01:10.280 --> 00:01:15.781
"In a few years, we hope you can enjoy the freedom we are fighting for."

16
00:01:17.422 --> 00:01:20.123
Just then, there was excitement in the street.

17
00:01:21.443 --> 00:01:24.424
Vinnie and Mandy ran to a window and looked out.

18
00:01:25.948 --> 00:01:30.110
A man was calling out in a loud voice as he walked down the street.

19
00:01:31.571 --> 00:01:33.471
Another man was beating a drum.

20
00:01:34.812 --> 00:01:37.873
People were coming out of their houses and following them.

21
00:01:37.893 --> 00:01:40.254
"Who is he?"

22
00:01:41.055 --> 00:01:41.755
asked Mandy.

23
00:01:41.775 --> 00:01:45.657
"The town crier," explained Paul Revere.

24
00:01:45.677 --> 00:01:48.298
"He is announcing a town meeting."

25
00:01:48.318 --> 00:01:52.920
"I think we should all attend," said John Adams.

26
00:01:54.532 --> 00:01:57.073
The children followed the men out of the house.

27
00:01:58.394 --> 00:01:59.734
Vinnie turned to Mandy.

28
00:01:59.754 --> 00:02:04.537
"I can't believe we just met these famous people!"

29
00:02:04.997 --> 00:02:05.477
he said.

30
00:02:06.698 --> 00:02:09.959
The townspeople gathered at a church and went inside.

31
00:02:11.540 --> 00:02:15.782
The place filled up quickly as people sat on the long, wooden benches.

32
00:02:17.322 --> 00:02:20.904
John Adams and Paul Revere walked to the front of the church.

33
00:02:22.268 --> 00:02:24.290
Will's father had just arrived.

34
00:02:25.791 --> 00:02:28.294
Vinnie, Mandy, and Will sat with him.

35
00:02:29.855 --> 00:02:31.477
"Welcome," said Adams.

36
00:02:31.497 --> 00:02:34.299
"We have many things to discuss.

37
00:02:35.580 --> 00:02:38.663
But first, most of you know what happened this morning."

38
00:02:38.683 --> 00:02:42.546
"They had no right to arrest John Hancock!"

39
00:02:43.167 --> 00:02:44.108
someone shouted.

40
00:02:45.349 --> 00:02:47.051
"We must do something, now!"

41
00:02:47.591 --> 00:02:48.392
yelled another.

42
00:02:50.128 --> 00:02:52.991
Vinnie and Mandy listened and watched closely.

43
00:02:54.392 --> 00:02:57.255
Everyone was allowed to say what he or she felt.

44
00:02:57.275 --> 00:03:03.640
"I say we should just pay the taxes," said one well-dressed man.

45
00:03:05.142 --> 00:03:06.723
Angry voices burst out.

46
00:03:06.743 --> 00:03:09.526
"Are you loyal to the British?"

47
00:03:10.026 --> 00:03:11.367
shouted an old man.

48
00:03:11.387 --> 00:03:16.232
"Let's not question each other's loyalty," said a young man.

49
00:03:17.332 --> 00:03:19.333
"We are all patriots!"

50
00:03:19.574 --> 00:03:21.215
"Please, please!"

51
00:03:21.795 --> 00:03:24.597
cried John Adams, raising both arms.

52
00:03:26.098 --> 00:03:27.519
The room quieted down.

53
00:03:27.539 --> 00:03:32.182
"Americans believe in freedom of speech," he said.

54
00:03:33.523 --> 00:03:35.164
People shouted in agreement.

55
00:03:35.184 --> 00:03:39.907
"But the British have no right to treat us this way!"

56
00:03:40.367 --> 00:03:42.068
yelled a man in a red vest.

57
00:03:43.589 --> 00:03:45.551
The room exploded in cheers.

58
00:03:48.704 --> 00:03:53.086
"There will be a war soon," said Will's father, shaking his head.

59
00:03:53.106 --> 00:03:56.508
"Maybe not, Father," said Will.

60
00:03:56.528 --> 00:04:00.109
"The British might allow us to have our freedom."

61
00:04:01.670 --> 00:04:02.750
Vinnie shook his head.

62
00:04:02.770 --> 00:04:05.391
"Your father is right, Will.

63
00:04:06.292 --> 00:04:07.632
There will be a war.

64
00:04:08.513 --> 00:04:09.353
Very soon."

65
00:04:10.554 --> 00:04:12.094
Mandy looked all around.

66
00:04:13.395 --> 00:04:15.536
The faces in the room were angry.

67
00:04:16.750 --> 00:04:19.186
Everyone was ready to fight for freedom.
